# Conventional Commits

Use [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) for every commit.

## Format

```
<type>(<scope>): <subject>

[optional body]
```

- **subject**: imperative, lowercase, no period, max ~72 chars
- **scope**: optional but preferred (`auth`, `market`, `gateway`, `websocket`, `frontend`, `shared`, `infra`, `deploy`)
- Never mention AI, Cursor, agents, or co-authors in messages

## Types

| Type | When to use |
|------|-------------|
| `feat` | New feature or user-facing capability |
| `fix` | Bug fix |
| `refactor` | Code change that is not a fix or feature |
| `chore` | Tooling, deps, config, CI, no production logic change |
| `docs` | Documentation only |
| `test` | Tests only |
| `perf` | Performance improvement |
| `build` | Build system or Docker changes |
| `ci` | CI/CD pipeline changes |

## Examples

```
feat(auth): add refresh token rotation with Redis sessions
fix(gateway): prepend http scheme for Render internal service URLs
refactor(market): extract Finnhub provider behind adapter interface
chore(infra): move FINNHUB_API_KEY to market-service in compose
docs: add Render deployment guide
test(auth): cover signup, refresh, and logout flows
```

## Phased commits

When changes span multiple areas, split into **logical phases** — one concern per commit:

1. Shared libraries / infrastructure
2. Individual microservices (auth → market → websocket → gateway)
3. Docker / env config
4. Frontend integration
5. Deployment / docs

Do not squash unrelated work into one commit. Do not commit `.DS_Store` or secrets.

## Push

Push after each phase or after a coherent batch. Use normal `git push` — no agent attribution in messages or trailers.
